-- R16 - KRW cards weigh the equity-flow channels, not exporter conversion alone (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Owner ask, 2 Nov 2026 (project thread "Add Korea equity flows to KRW cards").
-- Proposed 2 Nov 2026 ~03:00Z with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 8 Nov 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R16".
-- Body, title, evidence and revert_if below are byte-identical to the DB row (body md5 5b94543ed3a0026e9ce85532b7de35e1);
-- the rationale is generalised (the DB copy names cards and levels; this repo is public).
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R16' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "KRW cards weigh the equity-flow channels (foreign KOSPI flows and their hedges, resident retail and institutional outflows), not exporter conversion alone", "body": "KRW EQUITY-FLOW RULE (owner, 2 Nov 2026). Applies to every USDKRW / KRW-cross card (new card, review or BOOK CHECK) and to a KRW theme. Exporter conversion is one channel; Korea also has large equity-driven flows, and a card that cites only exporter, surplus or conversion logic fails the mechanism check until this line is printed.\n\n1. FOREIGN KOSPI FLOWS. Query msd.observations series KR.KRX_FOREIGN_NET_1D (Naver/KRX, units 100m won, so 10,000 = KRW 1tn): sum the last 5 and 20 sessions in KRW tn. Add today's intraday foreign net if the feeds or https://m.stock.naver.com/api/index/KOSPI/trend?bizdate=YYYYMMDD give it. Pressure estimate: about +0.09% on USDKRW per KRW 1tn of 5-day foreign net selling (weekly regression on our data, 6 months to 30 Oct 2026, corr -0.49, n 24; 2y slope -0.05, 2019-22 slope -0.33 when KOSPI was ~2.5x smaller). Print 'foreign KOSPI 5d <x>tn, 20d <y>tn -> ~<z>% USDKRW'. A divergence (5-day selling above KRW 5tn while USDKRW is flat or lower) means another flow is absorbing it; name the likelier one (exporter conversion, hedged holders lifting NDF hedges, NPS selling dollars) rather than calling the outflow irrelevant.\n2. FOREIGN HEDGE CHANNEL. Many foreign KOSPI holders hedge the won in the NDF. Equity selling that comes with an NDF volume spike in market pack section D (USDKRW NDF notional above 1.5x 20d) or a falling SGX KRW mini OI (FX_USDKRW.POS_SGX_KRW_MINI_OI, 5-day change) reads as hedges being lifted, roughly KRW-neutral; equity selling with quiet NDFs reads as unhedged money reaching spot. Equally, foreign buying into a KOSPI rally may be hedged and reach spot less than its size. Print one clause 'hedge read: <lifted / unhedged / no read>'. No tested read (R03): it explains, it does not raise p.\n3. RESIDENT OUTFLOWS. Retail: the latest monthly Korean retail overseas-equity net purchase (KSD SEIBro, reported by Yonhap, Korea Economic Daily or News1 in the first weeks of the next month; also domestic-listed US-equity ETF inflows such as TIGER / KODEX US funds) in USD bn with its month. Institutional: the latest dated news on NPS overseas allocation and hedging (strategic hedge ratio raised to 15% plus 5% tactical on 14 Apr 2026 near USDKRW 1,500; forward selling resumed June 2026; BoK-NPS FX swap line runs to end-2026), insurers' and lifers' hedge ratios, and BoK swap-line use. With USDKRW far below the levels where NPS hedges were put on, hedge rolls or a cut in the ratio are dollar buying; say which way any NPS news points. If no figure is found, print 'retail outflow: no figure' or 'NPS: nothing new', never a remembered number.\n4. NET LINE. Print 'KRW FLOWS: exporters <for/against/flat>; foreign equity <for/against>; hedge read <...>; retail outflow <$x bn mo-yy>; NPS/insurers <for/against/nothing new> -> net <supports/against/mixed> the card' (<=60 words) in the card's case against or the theme's Positioning line. If two or more equity channels point against the card, the case against must name them and the card must say why p still clears the gate; a card whose only support is exporter conversion while foreign equity and resident outflows both point against it is carded as thin edge at best.\n\nFOOTER: 'KRW flows: <n> cards checked'.", "rationale": "Owner, 2 Nov 2026, reviewing a Fable short-USDKRW card: Fable reasons from exporter flows only, but Korea has big equity-side flows (retail overseas outflows, institutional/NPS outflows, foreign hedging of Korean equity holdings) that need watching. [The DB copy of this field also names the cards and levels involved; removed here because this repo is public.]", "evidence": "Our data (msd.observations, Naver KRX foreign net vs Yahoo USDKRW close): weekly 5-day foreign net vs 5-day USDKRW % change, 6m corr -0.49 slope -0.093%/KRW tn (n 24); 2y corr -0.23 slope -0.054 (n 97); 2019-22 corr -0.38 slope -0.330 (n 197). Daily corr only -0.06 to -0.19, so the read is weekly, not daily. 15 Sep-15 Oct 2026 foreigners sold about KRW 32tn while USDKRW fell ~1,362 -> 1,341: something absorbed it. No retail-overseas or NPS series is in the database; those come from dated news.", "revert_if": "Revert or revise if by 15 Dec 2026 the KRW FLOWS line changed no KRW card (dead weight), or if the foreign-flow pressure estimate's sign is wrong on most weekly reviews.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-15", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
